%N A071487 Sprague-Grundy values for octal game .3077.
%C A071487 Octal games .244, .246, .254, and .256 have values a(n-1). - _Eric M. Schmidt_, Feb 09 2017
%C A071487 From _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Jul 30 2026: (Start)
%C A071487 a(n) is also the Sprague-Grundy value of a heap of n+1 tokens in the octal game .244; equivalently, the Sprague-Grundy sequence of .244 is 0, 0, followed by this sequence.
%C A071487 Computed (as the game .244) through heap size 2^28 = 268435456 by Tyler Satchel Orden (2026), extending A. Flammenkamp's tables for .244, which reached 2^27: 65367 rare values in Flammenkamp's sparse-space sense, the last at heap size 7596617; the maximum value grows to 7230, first attained at heap size 202510574. Flammenkamp's published invariants at 2^27 were reproduced exactly before extending. (End)
%D A071487 E. R. Berlekamp, J. H. Conway and R. K. Guy, Winning Ways, Academic Press, NY, 2 vols., 1982; see Chapter 4.
